{"title":"2003 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Several figures can be made by attaching two equilateral triangles to the regular pentagon ABCDE in two of the five positions shown. How many non-congruent figures can be constructed in this way?\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/b/a3b1113e62996ab9b1c6c83bc4836bbb32070801.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(200); defaultpen(0.9); real r = 5/dir(54).x, h = 5 tan(54*pi/180); pair A = (5,0), B = A+10*dir(72), C = (0,r+h), E = (-5,0), D = E+10*dir(108); draw(A--B--C--D--E--cycle); label(&quot;\\(A\\)&quot;,A+(0,-0.5),SSE); label(&quot;\\(B\\)&quot;,B+(0.5,0),ENE); label(&quot;\\(C\\)&quot;,C+(0,0.5),N); label(&quot;\\(D\\)&quot;,D+(-0.5,0),WNW); label(&quot;\\(E\\)&quot;,E+(0,-0.5),SW); // real l = 5*sqrt(3); pair ab = (h+l)*dir(72), bc = (h+l)*dir(54); pair AB = (ab.y, h-ab.x), BC = (bc.x,h+bc.y), CD = (-bc.x,h+bc.y), DE = (-ab.y, h-ab.x), EA = (0,-l); draw(A--AB--B^^B--BC--C^^C--CD--D^^D--DE--E^^E--EA--A, dashed); // dot(A); dot(B); dot(C); dot(D); dot(E); dot(AB); dot(BC); dot(CD); dot(DE); dot(EA); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"318\" /></center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/b/0eb89b0c6e9882236266b9c5d9b6da4c6890ae6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text {(A) } 1 \\qquad \\text {(B) } 2 \\qquad \\text {(C) } 3 \\qquad \\text {(D) } 4 \\qquad \\text {(E) } 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"330\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Place the first triangle. Now, we can place the second triangle either adjacent to the first, or with one side between them, for a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a167bd0ffda41b60ae5177713726594798a86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(B) }2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"51\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/c/96c9544caef563e6ec7efdf92aa0071947f7006f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${5 \\choose 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"33\" height=\"53\" /> to realize there are 10 ways to choose 2 different triangles. Then divide by 5 for each vertex of a pentagon to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a167bd0ffda41b60ae5177713726594798a86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(B) }2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"51\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B\">2003 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"